remain an external user action; deleting files in a later commit would not
remove a secret from already published history.

Commit `ff4ef3e9ebfa084ac57c1c1064bea6baafa9f26c` was the
pre-acceptance parent HEAD and pre-push remote HEAD. Any correction must be a
forward commit after final verification: no force-push, reset, history rewrite,
silent conflict resolution, or destructive cleanup.

## Verification contract

The final direct checks are:

1. parse the top manifest as JSON;
2. reconstruct and exactly cover the Git delta;
3. verify every live and base-blob byte size and SHA-256;
4. recursively validate all nine lower receipts and every imported destination;
5. verify required landmarks and exact semantic-group counts;
6. run the focused manifest test and Ruff on the direct test;
7. inspect the final diff for only the three leased top-freeze paths.

Passing these checks establishes package structure and provenance only. Push
authorization remains false until the parent coordinator performs final Git
acceptance and the security hold is resolved.
